{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The circuit's power is $0$ when $P(c)=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\nP(c)\u0026=0\n\\\\\\\\\n-20(c-3)^2+180\u0026=0\n\\\\\\\\\n-20(c-3)^2\u0026=-180\n\\\\\\\\\n(c-3)^2\u0026=9\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{(c-3)^2}\u0026=\\sqrt{9}\n\\\\\\\\\nc-3\u0026=\\pm3\n\\\\\\\\\nc\u0026=\\pm3+3\n\\\\\\\\\nc=6\u0026\\text{ or }c=0\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, these are the currents that will produce no power:\n\nLower current: $0$ amperes\n\nHigher current: $6$ amperes","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"The power generated by an electrical circuit (in watts) as a function of its current $c$ (in amperes) is modeled by:\n\n$P(c)=-20(c-3)^2+180$\n\n**Which currents will produce no power (i.e. $0$ watts)?**  \n*Enter the lower current first.*\n\nLower current: [[☃ numeric-input 1]] amperes\n\nHigher current: [[☃ numeric-input 2]] amperes","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":0}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"lower current","multipleNumberInput":false,"rightAlign":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"numeric-input 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":6}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"higher current","multipleNumberInput":false,"rightAlign":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
